@* Privacy Policy in English. The Bulgarian version is Privacy.cshtml: a change goes into both files. *@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<article class="tg-legal">
    <header class="tg-page-head">
        <div>
            <h1 class="tg-page-head__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="tg-page-head__sub">Last updated: 01.11.2026</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>1. Who processes your data</h2>
        <p>The controller of your personal data is:</p>
        <partial name="_LegalOperator" />
        <p>For questions and requests about your personal data, write through "Contact the organisers" in your profile or to the e-mail address above.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account:</strong> first name, last name, e-mail and password (we keep only an encrypted fingerprint of the password, not the password itself).</li>
            <li><strong>Coach:</strong> the name you enter and your years of experience. <strong>Referee:</strong> name, date of birth (to check the age) and years of experience.</li>
            <li><strong>Team:</strong> the team name and the players' names entered by the coach.</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Payments:</strong> amount, status, dates, the payment identifiers at Stripe, the language of the payment,
                and when and from which IP address the participation declaration was accepted. Card details are entered directly
                at Stripe and never reach us.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Activity on the website:</strong> ratings of and comments on referees, messages to the organisers, notifications.</li>
            <li><strong>Pictures</strong> from the tournaments in the gallery.</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Technical data:</strong> cookies (see section 7); the IP address used to limit sign-in attempts (kept only
                in the server's memory for a few minutes); the server logs at the hosting provider.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. What we use it for and on what legal basis</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Account, entering tournaments, running them and the messages about them (e-mail confirmation, password reset,
                payment, reminder, cancellation, change of date) – <em>performance of the contract</em> (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
            </li>
            <li>
                Payments, refunds and accounting records – <em>the contract</em> and a <em>legal obligation</em> under accounting
                and tax law (Art. 6(1)(b) and (c)).
            </li>
            <li>
                E-mails about new tournaments – <em>your consent</em> (Art. 6(1)(a)). You give it with a tick when registering or
                in "My Profile", and you can withdraw it at any time – in your profile or with the link in every such e-mail.
            </li>
            <li>
                Results and rankings, the names of coaches and referees (for signed-in users), ratings and comments, pictures
                from the tournaments – our <em>legitimate interest</em> in presenting the tournaments (Art. 6(1)(f)). You can
                object (section 8).
            </li>
            <li>Protection against abuse (limiting sign-in attempts, locking accounts after wrong passwords) – <em>legitimate interest</em>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Who sees the data</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>All visitors:</strong> team names, results, rankings and the pictures in the gallery.</li>
            <li><strong>Signed-in users:</strong> also the coaches' names in the rankings, the referees' names, and the ratings of and comments on them (with the author's name).</li>
            <li><strong>The organisers:</strong> the data needed to run the tournaments and to answer messages.</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Processors acting for us:</strong> Stripe (payments; Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd., Ireland), Google
                (sending e-mails through Gmail) and the hosting provider where the website and its database are kept. Stripe and
                Google may also process data in the USA – based on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses.
            </li>
            <li>We do not sell data or use it for advertising. We give it to public authorities only when the law requires it.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Your account and the data linked to it – until you delete the account. Deleting it removes the account, its
                roles, the players, your messages, ratings and comments; the team name stays only in tournaments already
                played and in the rankings.
            </li>
            <li>Payments – as long as accounting and tax law require, also after the account is deleted.</li>
            <li>Pictures – until you ask for them to be taken down or until the tournament is deleted.</li>
            <li>Technical records of sent e-mails – up to 24 hours after sending.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>6. Security</h2>
        <p>
            The website works only over a secure connection (HTTPS), passwords are stored encrypted, and access to the data is
            limited to the organisers.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
        <p>The website uses only necessary cookies – no analytics or advertising cookies – so it does not ask for consent to them:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>.AspNetCore.Identity.Application</code> – keeps you signed in;</li>
            <li><code>.AspNetCore.Antiforgery.*</code> – protects the forms against forgery;</li>
            <li><code>.AspNetCore.Culture</code> – the language you chose (1 year);</li>
            <li><code>.AspNetCore.Mvc.CookieTempDataProvider</code> – short messages between two pages.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Stripe's payment page uses its own cookies under Stripe's rules.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            You have the right to access your data, to have it corrected, to have it erased (you can delete your account
            yourself in "My Profile"), to restrict processing, to data portability, to object to processing based on legitimate
            interest (for example a picture or your name in the rankings), and to withdraw your consent at any time. Write
            through "Contact the organisers" or to the e-mail address above – we answer within one month.
        </p>
        <p>
            You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection: 2 Prof.
            Tsvetan Lazarov Blvd., 1592 Sofia, <a href="https://www.cpdp.bg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cpdp.bg</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>9. Children</h2>
        <p>
            Accounts can be created by persons aged 18 or over. The names of players under 18 are entered by the coach with
            their parents' consent and are not shown publicly. We remove a picture of a child at a parent's request.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may change this policy. The current version is always on this page.</p>
    </section>
</article>
